---
title: "Learn with us on the browser - AmpliLearn and MetaLearn now available to explore!"
date: 2026-07-21
---

We have released two browser-based tools to explore some of the work that we do here at the MEEG lab. If you are a beginner to microbiome research I invite you to learn from AmpliLearn and MetaLearn how to conduct envirionmental community analysis using various bioinformatics tools.
AmpliLearn is a concise step by step run through how to analyse 16S and ITS amplicon data. With this tool you can upload your OTU x Sample matrix and visualise your data preliminarily to gain some insights before running the analysis thoroughly.
MetaLearn on the other hand simulates metagenome analysis which often requires quite a lot of computing power, but is a more thorough exploration of the microbiome. 


